{"reference":"Genesis 18","book":"Genesis","chapter":18,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Sarah in scriptural reception","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Sarah's obedience and her use of lord language belong to scriptural reception and household rhetoric. The supplied context does not make all women daughters only through deference to men, nor does it establish male superiority; those broader conclusions go beyond the cited disputed material.","verse_refs":["Genesis 18:12"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_018_6279be02ec4c8424c60af281"],"confidence":"low","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
